    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504-a2">

                <pb facs="0796" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1885/pg668"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I am directed by the President of
                    the United States to convey to your excellency his most sincere thanks, and
                    those of the people of the United States, for the distinguished and most
                    opportune services rendered by you to the survivors of the Jeannette Arctic
                    exploring expedition and to the relief parties sent out in search of them, which
                    were, thus enabled to accomplish the objects of their sad mission.</p>
                <p>The President likewise begs your acceptance of the accompanying sword as a
                    further testimonial of the enduring gratitude of the American people and their
                    Chief Magistrate for your excellency’s powerful and valuable assistance in time
                    of need.</p>
                <p>With best wishes for your excellency’s continued health and welfare, be pleased
                    to accept the assurances of my most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>His excellency Maj. Gen. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Georgf
                            Tchernaieff</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Governor of Yakutsk,
                            Siberia.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
